OL,3,ATax banks to cut energy bills, unions
OL,4,Atell Burnham
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe leader of Britain's trade unionists
OL,7,Fhas told Andy Burnham the government
OL,8,Fshould introduce a "social tariff",
OL,9,Fpaid for by a bank surcharge, to help
OL,10,Flow and middle earners with their
OL,11,Fenergy bills.
OL,13,FA social tariff is a discount on bills
OL,14,Fbased on household income, and the TUC
OL,15,Fsays it believes two-thirds of
OL,16,Fhouseholds could benefit.
OL,18,FThe TUC says the bank surcharge, which
OL,19,Fwas reduced in 2023 from 8% to 3% by
OL,20,Fthe then Conservative government,
OL,21,Fshould be reversed - and estimates it
OL,22,Fwould raise #9bn over four years.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
